// Title: Usage Of Web Request Commands And Cmdlets
// ID: 9fc51a3c-81b3-4fa7-b35f-7c02cf10fd2d
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: James Pemberton / @4A616D6573, Endgame, JHasenbusch, oscd.community, Austin Songer @austinsonger
// Date: 2019-10-24
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
// Description: Detects the use of various web request commands with commandline tools and Windows PowerShell cmdlets (including aliases) via CommandLine
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

_sourceCategory=* | where ((CommandLine matches "*[System.Net.WebRequest]::create*" or CommandLine matches "*curl *" or CommandLine matches "*Invoke-RestMethod*" or CommandLine matches "*Invoke-WebRequest*" or CommandLine matches "* irm *" or CommandLine matches "*iwr *" or CommandLine matches "*Resume-BitsTransfer*" or CommandLine matches "*Start-BitsTransfer*" or CommandLine matches "*wget *" or CommandLine matches "*WinHttp.WinHttpRequest*"))
